{
  "finding": "Scene S005 depicts an honor guard firing rifle volleys during an outdoor funeral service. Under Industry-Wide Labor-Management Safety Committee Safety Bulletin #1 guidelines, before any firearm is used, the production must conduct a safety meeting with all involved personnel to review safety issues, including an on-site walk-through and/or dry run, and issue protective shields, eye and hearing protection, or other appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) to all personnel in close proximity or directly in the line of fire. Script action does not establish whether practical firearms or blanks will be used on set, and actual production methods remain unconfirmed.",
  "remedy_detail": "If live or blank-firing firearms are utilized on set, conduct a safety meeting with all involved personnel to review relevant safety issues, including an on-site walk-through or dry run, and ensure appropriate PPE such as hearing and eye protection is issued and used by personnel in close proximity or in the line of fire. Alternatively, eliminate on-set live blank discharges entirely by using non-firing replica rifles or rubber props, adding muzzle flashes, smoke, and audio volley sound effects during post-production. Confirm the planned shooting method, staging, and prop choices with the production team.",
  "remedy_action": "REPLACE",
  "severity": "HIGH"
}

